## OpenInference fixes ignored environment settings for hiding trace content

Source: Arize AI / OpenInference — https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference/releases/tag/%40arizeai/openinference-core%402.8.1
Published: 2026-10-23
Channel: github

OpenInference adds AI-specific records to application traces, including model inputs and outputs. Its JavaScript core package has fixed a configuration path that could leave content-masking settings inactive. In version 2.8.1, the configuration generator reads OPENINFERENCE_* environment variables when instrumentation is created without an explicit traceConfig object. Previously, that path returned hard-coded defaults. The release specifically identifies OPENINFERENCE_HIDE_INPUTS=true and other masking variables as having no effect in that situation.

For illustration, a service owner might set the input-hiding variable in a deployment manifest and assume prompts will be withheld. If the instrumentor relies on the affected default configuration path, that expectation would not match the recorded trace. This is a telemetry privacy correction, rather than a change to the model request itself.

Engineers maintaining JavaScript instrumentation should check the installed core version and inspect a fresh trace after upgrading. The release does not establish which deployments retained sensitive content, and it does not promise to remove previously stored records. Explicit configuration and environment-driven configuration should each be tested against the application’s actual construction path.

Why it matters: Teams relying on environment variables to hide prompts should verify a fresh trace and review whether earlier records need attention under their retention policy.

