## DigitalOcean adds a dashboard for prompt-cache hit rates and savings

Source: DigitalOcean — https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/now-available-prompt-caching
Published: 2026-10-23
Channel: news

DigitalOcean’s Serverless Inference runs model requests without requiring customers to operate the serving infrastructure. Its prompt-caching announcement adds a dashboard for checking whether repeated context is actually being reused. Caching avoids processing an unchanged prompt prefix again, but that benefit depends on a request reaching a replica that holds the cached context. The company describes routing requests toward replicas with the largest matching prefix before balancing load within that group.

The new control-panel dashboard shows hit rate over time, a breakdown by model and estimated dollars saved. Responses report cached and uncached token counts, including on the Responses API. For illustration, a team running a support agent can compare these counts with its repeated system instructions before assuming that a longer conversation receives a discount. A low hit rate gives engineers a concrete signal to investigate.

DigitalOcean advertises discounts of up to 90 percent and time-to-first-token reductions of up to 80 percent, with results varying by model and prompt. Its reported hit rates come from internal testing. An optional prompt_cache_key separates cache groups within an account; it does not pin requests to one replica. These qualifications make workload-specific measurement more useful than treating headline savings as guaranteed.

Why it matters: Teams using DigitalOcean inference should compare the dashboard with response token counts and measured latency for their own workload before budgeting savings.

